```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Self-hosted long-horizon tool-agent builders with verbose tool outputs (code search, web fetch, DB rows) where context token cost dominates and model attention scores are accessible; IF real traces validate the sparse+predictable reference pattern (unproven in L0).
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbench-only. L0 is a trace simulation with synthetic salience proxy and span-availability success metric—no real model, no real task accuracy, no measurement on production tool outputs. The +0.514 EC−RT win at budget 0.25 and zero oracle gap in the favorable regime are simulation artifacts; operational survival vs a paged kernel (vLLM/SGLang PagedAttention) plus existing attention-based KV eviction (H2O, SnapKV) is unproven.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Requires model-internal attention/citation signal—unavailable via standard APIs; must build span tracking, scoring, and eviction into the agent loop; competes with H2O/SnapKV (already integrated in vLLM/SGLang) and prompt compression (LLMLingua) which are model-agnostic; sparsity/predictability of real tool outputs is assumed, not verified; tool-result-specific structure limits generality to non-tool prompts; long-context windows (128k–1M) and PagedAttention reduce the urgency of extractive compression]
RATIONALE: Packet admits "This is a TRACE SIMULATION, not a model run" and "task-success = referenced-span availability, a proxy; the salience score is a SYNTHETIC stand-in for real attention/citation signal" (RESULTS.md). Oracle-vs-causal gap is exactly zero only in the "FAVORABLE (sparse 0.02 + high-pred)" regime (gap 0.000, CI [0,0]); in the hostile dense+low-pred regime the gap is +0.119 (CI [+0.091,+0.148]), showing the win is regime-gated. Prior-art caveat lists "LLMLingua (prompt compression), H2O & SnapKV (attention-based KV-cache eviction), StreamingLLM (recency + attention-sink truncation, ≈ our RT arm)" as a crowded field; the only claimed distinct angle is "(a) TOOL-RESULT-specific + (b) retention-as-causal-future-reference-prediction with the oracle gap quantified" (RESULTS.md). No evidence is provided that the EC policy beats H2O/SnapKV on real attention, or that production tool outputs exhibit the sparse+predictable reference pattern. The honest negative (N3 refuted in sim, but gap opens in hostile regime) is actionable: do not deploy where references are dense/unpredictable or where attention signal is unavailable.
```
